# Documentation discipline

Documentation is part of implementation, not a separate optional step.

## When to update

- Update existing documentation when behavior, commands, or paths change.
- Prefer editing `README.md` and files under `docs/` over creating new documents.
- Remove or fix stale documentation when you find it.

## When not to create docs

- Do not create new documentation without a clear long-term purpose.
- Do not duplicate the same explanation across many files — link instead.
- Never document commands, flags, or paths that do not exist.

## Style

- Use simple B2 English.
- Explain why, not only what.
- Keep examples copy-paste friendly.
- Keep `README.md` concise. Put detailed guides under `docs/`.

## Project vs global docs

- Global container rules guide agent behavior in every session.
- Project rules (`/workspace/.cursor/`, `AGENTS.md`) belong to the mounted repository.
- Do not move project-specific stack or architecture rules into global defaults.
